Mark XXIII: the living reply (streamed dashboard + spoken answers)

The console showed only final replies; now it streams like the CLI.

- dashboard.py: the turn worker passes an on_text_delta callback to the
  agent (streaming path when the brain supports it, fallback otherwise)
  and pushes throttled "partial" events - one per 0.4s, not per token -
  so the event cap stays meaningful (raised 600 -> 1200).
- dashboard_page.py: a streaming bubble renders each partial with a
  caret and is replaced by the final reply event; the SPEAK toggle uses
  the browser's own speechSynthesis (on-device, no audio leaves the
  machine), strips markdown/code blocks before speaking, skips error
  replies, and remembers the preference in localStorage.
- Tests: streaming round-trip with FakeStreamChain - partials arrive,
  grow monotonically, and the final reply matches; page carries the
  streaming + speechSynthesis + SPEAK hooks.
- Version 3.10.0.
